<title>USA: Ride Inc Q3 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Ride Inc Q3 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>PRESTON, Wash. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>Three months ended Sept. 30,  Nine months ended Sept. 30,</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	  1996	   1995</p>
<p> Net sales	   $35,329   $31,896     $61,606	$49,160</p>
<p>Cost of goods sold</p>
<p>			  23,985    22,795	42,712	 35,983</p>
<p> Gross profit	 11,344     9,101	18,894	 13,177</p>
<p>Selling, general</p>
<p>and administrative</p>
<p>  expenses	     5,419     3,525	14,090	  6,954</p>
<p> Operating income    5,925     5,576	 4,804	  6,223</p>
<p>Interest income</p>
<p>  (expense)	    (111)	 114	   140	    276</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>  income taxes	 5,814     5,690	 4,944	  6,499</p>
<p> Income tax expense  2,172     2,113	 1,874	  2,417</p>
<p> Net income	    3,642     3,577	 3,070	  4,082</p>
<p>Per share:</p>
<p>   Primary		0.32	0.34	  0.27	   0.42</p>
<p>   Fully diluted	0.32	0.33	  0.27	   0.40</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares outstanding:</p>
<p>   Primary	    11,258    10,548	11,334	  9,550</p>
<p>   Fully diluted    11,485    10,832	11,534	 10,159</p>
